      "message": "Comments from Behzad:\n1. In battery only mode, turn off PSYS will turn on a lot macros inside of the IC to save power, for example, with PSYS disabled, the current consumption of the IC is around 20uA, while with PSYS enabled, the current consumption of the IC is around 1.3mA. \n2. We need to disable the PSYS when we are not providing power through all USB ports and IMVP is off (VGG, VCORE and VSA). This is in S5 and lower states.",
